 "evidenceBoundary": {
  "exact": "The selected installed native hashes, six .pdata windows including the routine entry/continuations/epilogue and two formatter windows, branch targets, both record allocations, nine literal loads, nine formatter-to-helper forwarding sequences, packed tile argument extraction, formatter argument stores and both collection appends are checked byte-for-byte.",
  "direct": "The selected UnityPlayer routine enters before the path-building window, continues through it, and reaches a shared epilogue. It groups LAYER_C/D/N paths in one 32-byte record appended under owner +0x70. A separate 56-byte record stores a packed tile argument at +0, forwards Terrain_H/N/T/A/S/C paths into six result slots at +8 through +48, and appends under owner +0xC0. The tile argument splits into high 4, middle 14 and low 14 bits; the selected formatter helper builds a contiguous root, high, low, middle argument vector and forwards it through a checked bridge.",
  "unresolved": "Neither grouped path record identifies decoded channel roles, VirtualTextureRenderer bindings, layer compositing, live selection or rendering. The six Terrain templates and the layer templates are different path/record families."
